      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The significant and increasing latency spikes at hops 3 and 4 strongly suggest a link saturation or congestion issue, rather than a classic routing loop. Routing loops usually result in consistently high latency or repeated addresses in the trace. The erratic nature of the jitter points toward buffer overflows on a congested router or switch along that path. Further investigation should involve checking CPU load and interface queue statistics on the devices at hops 3 and 4.",
      "source": "target",
